assertion  XSH.iswalnum.001
anchor     functions/iswalnum.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswalnum.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswalnum() returns non-zero for each character
           of the class alnum as the locale definition lists it: the 26
           uppercase letters, the 26 lowercase letters and the ten digits.
test       t/001-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswalnum.002
anchor     functions/iswalnum.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswalnum.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswalnum() returns 0 for each of these
           characters, which the locale definition does not place in the
           class: the 32 punctuation characters, the six white-space
           characters, and the other control characters.
test       t/002-non-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswalnum.003
anchor     functions/iswalnum.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswalnum.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       iswalnum(WEOF) is within the domain and returns 0, since WEOF is
           not a character of the class.
test       t/003-weof.c

assertion  XSH.iswalnum.004
anchor     functions/iswalnum.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswalnum.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       For each of the 128 characters (portable printable set plus the
           control characters), iswalnum() is non-zero exactly when iswalpha()
           or iswdigit() is non-zero.
test       t/004-alnum-is-alpha-or-digit.c

assertion  XSH.iswalnum.005
anchor     functions/iswalnum.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswalnum.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In a UTF-8 locale, iswalnum() is still non-zero for the 52 letters
           and ten digits.
note       Needs an installed multibyte UTF-8 locale (NOTINUSE otherwise);
           only ASCII-range characters are examined.
test       t/005-utf8-portable.c
